--- body ---

## Context

Step D of 0978. Run the whole cutover end to end in a disposable HOME seeded with a copy of
the repository, before touching the live one. Extends the 2026-09-28 rollback prototype
(23 crash points) from fixture to full shape.

Traps the rehearsal must cover: every worktree's `.git` file holds an absolute
`gitdir: $HOME/.claude/.git/worktrees/...` (needs `git worktree repair`); the
cwd-keyed project memory and `~/.claude.json` entries (0984's remedy); the per-entry links
one level down in `projects/*/memory`; the systemd timers, especially `claude-refresh`
which pulls `~/.claude` daily.

## Exit criteria

Reworded 2026-09-29 by author decision (PR #1067): a manual runbook with a tar-snapshot
rollback replaces the two scripts and the crash-point rehearsal.

- [x] A runbook for the live window is written (`docs/idh-cutover-checklist.md`), covering: quiet-window preconditions (no sessions, clean tree, no worktree needed mid-flight); a tar snapshot of `~/.claude`, `~/.claude.json` and `~/.idh` taken first; pausing and resuming `claude-refresh.timer`, `idh-mammoth-audit.timer` and `claude-telemetry-prune.timer`; the move, the per-entry links, `git worktree repair`, the `projects/<slug>` rename and the `~/.claude.json` re-key
- [x] Rollback is restoring that snapshot, and the runbook says how
- [x] The runbook includes a census of `~/.claude/.git/worktrees` for stale registrations before the move
- [x] Verification is named: `idh check`, the validator before the first launch (the unrewritten manifest refusing as the expected control), a fresh session per runtime, and the negative control
- [x] The findings of the abandoned scripted attempt are carried as warnings: slug look-alikes, `projects/` keys in `~/.claude.json`, `XDG_STATE_HOME`, the three `git status` entries of the memory rename, refusing before mutating

Superseded (no longer required): one cutover and one rollback script, idempotent, with a
disposable-HOME crash-point rehearsal; the scripted manifest rewrite (it moves to runbook
step 9 and stays in 0986's criteria).
